<section class="growth-section container">
  <div class="section-intro">
    <p class="eyebrow"><%- icon('trending-up', { size: 13 }) %> Live from Crowdwide</p>
    <h2>The numbers,<br><em>not a model.</em></h2>
    <p class="section-copy">Crowdwide's feed reserves a fixed share of every "For you" page for people and communities outside your existing network, so a good post doesn't depend on already being popular. These charts are computed from real published posts in public communities over the last <%= growthStats.weeks %> weeks (private communities are never counted) and refresh every few minutes.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="growth-grid">
    <div class="growth-card">
      <div class="growth-card-head">
        <h3>Reach: new vs. established communities</h3>
        <p>Average views per post, grouped by the week the post went up.</p>
      </div>
      <%- include('growth-chart-svg', { chart: growthStats.reach, weeks: growthStats.weeks, unit: 'views per post', label: 'Line chart of average views per post by week, comparing posts in communities under 30 days old with posts in established communities.' }) %>
      <p class="growth-caption">Based on <%= growthStats.totals.newCommunityPosts.toLocaleString() %> posts in new communities and <%= growthStats.totals.establishedPosts.toLocaleString() %> in established ones. Views keep accumulating after a post goes up, so compare the two lines within the same week rather than across weeks.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="growth-card">
      <div class="growth-card-head">
        <h3>Activity by community size</h3>
        <p>Average posts per community per week, grouped by current member count.</p>
      </div>
      <%- include('growth-chart-svg', { chart: growthStats.size, weeks: growthStats.weeks, unit: 'posts per community', label: 'Line chart of average posts per community per week for intermediate versus large public communities.' }) %>
      <p class="growth-caption"><%= growthStats.totals.intermediateCommunities.toLocaleString() %> intermediate and <%= growthStats.totals.largeCommunities.toLocaleString() %> large public communities out of <%= growthStats.totals.communities.toLocaleString() %> in total. Updated <%= growthStats.updatedAt.toLocaleString('en', { dateStyle: 'medium', timeStyle: 'short', timeZone: 'UTC' }) %> UTC.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
